prompt:
VALIDATION LEVEL: FAST

Read the existing orchestrator implementation and operating protocol.
Do not re-read unrelated research/data files unless required.

OBJECTIVE

Improve Stock Research Lab monitoring using telemetry exposed by the
installed Codex SDK / underlying App Server.

Current problems:

- actual Model displays N/A;
- token usage displays N/A;
- requested model tier is sometimes missing from Codex final reports;
- we cannot distinguish Codex/model time from slow local execution time.

This is a SMALL infrastructure job.
Do not modify research contracts, historical data, or research methodology.

PRIORITY 1 — ACTUAL MODEL

Determine from the installed openai-codex SDK and underlying App Server
events/metadata how to obtain the actual model used for a turn.

Do not guess.

Persist when available:

- requested model_tier;
- resolved/requested model identifier;
- actual runtime model identifier;
- reasoning effort.

Clearly distinguish requested/resolved model from runtime-confirmed model.

If actual runtime model is genuinely unavailable, preserve N/A and document
the exact limitation.

PRIORITY 2 — TOKEN USAGE

Inspect SDK/App Server turn/event telemetry for real token usage.

Capture only values actually exposed by the runtime.

Where available persist:

- current turn input tokens;
- current turn output tokens;
- current turn total tokens;
- current job cumulative tokens;
- today's cumulative tokens for jobs recorded by THIS orchestrator only.

Do NOT estimate values.
Do NOT infer ChatGPT Pro weekly quota.
Do NOT fabricate missing token counts.

If App Server exposes cached/reasoning token detail cheaply, preserve it only
if straightforward. Do not expand scope merely to obtain optional detail.

PRIORITY 3 — ELAPSED / LOCAL EXECUTION TIMING

Persist lightweight timing sufficient to identify PC-side bottlenecks:

- job start;
- Codex turn start/end;
- total elapsed;
- local command/tool execution duration when runtime events expose it;
- test-command duration when identifiable.

Do not build a profiler.

Aggregate only useful high-level values.

PRIORITY 4 — MONITOR

Keep:

    python -m orchestrator monitor

Extend its concise display approximately to:

Stock Research Lab Monitor

Current Job
  ID
  Status
  Model Tier
  Requested Model
  Actual Model
  Reasoning
  Sandbox
  Thread
  Elapsed

Usage
  Turn input
  Turn output
  Turn total
  Job total
  Today total

Execution
  Codex elapsed
  Local command elapsed
  Test elapsed

Recent Activity
  ...

Display N/A for unavailable values.

Do not make the monitor continuously refresh by default.
Preserve one-shot behavior.

PRIORITY 5 — EVENT COLLECTION

Prefer using the existing Python SDK/App Server integration rather than
launching a second independent Codex process.

If the Python SDK already exposes sufficient event/turn metadata, use it.

If direct App Server event subscription is required:

- keep the integration minimal;
- reuse the SDK-managed Codex runtime where practical;
- do not build a generalized App Server client;
- do not build a web UI;
- do not add a database;
- do not add a daemon/service;
- do not add a queue.

Do not duplicate Codex turns merely to collect telemetry.

PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENT

Telemetry must not materially slow normal jobs.

Avoid:

- repeated repository scans;
- expensive log parsing;
- polling loops;
- large event archives;
- storing full command output merely for telemetry.

Persist compact structured telemetry only.

FAIL-SAFE REQUIREMENT

Telemetry failure must NOT cause a successful research/Codex job to fail.

If telemetry cannot be collected:

- record N/A;
- record a concise telemetry warning;
- preserve the actual job result.

SECURITY

Never capture or persist:

- .env contents;
- credentials;
- authentication tokens;
- Telegram session contents;
- brokerage/account information;
- secret environment-variable values.

Command telemetry must avoid persisting secret-bearing command arguments or
environment dumps.

MODEL POLICY

Preserve the existing four-tier policy:

economy   -> Luna
standard  -> Terra
advanced  -> Sol
critical  -> Astra

Do not change model policy in this job.

Do not enable xhigh automatically.

TESTS — FAST ONLY

Run only orchestrator/telemetry/monitor tests affected by this change.

Add focused tests for:

1. requested/resolved/actual model distinction;
2. actual-model N/A fallback;
3. real token telemetry persistence when supplied;
4. token N/A fallback;
5. job/day aggregation from recorded usage;
6. elapsed timing;
7. monitor rendering;
8. telemetry failure does not fail the job;
9. secret values are not persisted.

Do NOT run the entire research test suite.

Run git diff --check.

DOCUMENTATION

Update only the relevant orchestrator documentation.

Document exactly which telemetry comes from:

- job specification;
- SDK;
- App Server/runtime events;
- local orchestrator timing.

Document any unavailable fields.

FINAL RESPONSE

Be concise.

Report:

- requested model tier;
- resolved/requested model;
- whether actual runtime model is now available;
- which token fields are now available;
- which timing fields are available;
- files changed;
- focused tests and duration;
- telemetry overhead/limitations;
- recommended next step.

Do not commit or push.
